{"type": "answer", "run_id": "retrieval-part2-lean-20261110", "scenario": "eval:retrieval", "source": "real", "setting": "small_lean", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 600, "k": 4, "rerank": false, "router": false}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q3", "request_id": "retrieval-part2-lean-20261110-small_lean-gpt-oss-120b-Q3", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:25:27.673+00:00", "degraded": false, "reply": {"request_id": "retrieval-part2-lean-20261110-small_lean-gpt-oss-120b-Q3", "question": "How are the positional encodings built, and why sinusoids rather than learned embeddings?", "kind": "answer", "level": 0, "text": "The Transformer adds a positional encoding vector of the same dimension \\(d_{model}\\) to each token embedding, where each entry of the encoding is defined by a sinusoid that depends on the token’s position \\(pos\\) and the dimension index \\(i\\) [S1]. Specifically, for even dimensions the value is \\(\\sin(pos/10000^{2i/d_{model}})\\) and for odd dimensions it is \\(\\cos(pos/10000^{2i/d_{model}})\\), giving a set of sinusoids with wavelengths that form a geometric progression from \\(2\\pi\\) to \\(10000·2\\pi\\) [S4]. The authors also tried learned positional embeddings, but found performance essentially identical to the sinusoidal version [S3]. They preferred the sinusoidal encodings because the fixed functions make it easy for the model to represent relative positions as linear combinations and because they may enable the model to extrapolate to sequence lengths longer than seen during training [S3][S4].", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "1706.03762v7 p.6 §3.5", "pid": "attention:600:0033", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p06-b004", "attention-p06-b005"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "1706.03762v7 p.8 §5.4", "pid": "attention:600:0049", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p08-b003", "attention-p08-b004"]}, {"sid": "S3", "cite": "1706.03762v7 p.6 §3.5", "pid": "attention:600:0035", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p06-b009"]}, {"sid": "S4", "cite": "1706.03762v7 p.6 §3.5", "pid": "attention:600:0034", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p06-b006", "attention-p06-b007", "attention-p06-b008"]}], "notice": "checked for citations only (no second-model check)", "eta_s": null, "model_calls": [{"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 761, "completion_tokens": 261, "tokens_estimated": false, "ms": 968.4205000012298, "waited_s": 6.141}], "spans": [{"name": "plan", "start_ms": 0.0, "end_ms": 0.9, "model": null, "outcome": "full", "detail": {"predicted_wait_s": {"full": {"openai/gpt-oss-120b": 6.139426310000999}}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b"}}, {"name": "understand", "start_ms": 0.9, "end_ms": 0.9, "model": null, "outcome": "off (config)", "detail": {}}, {"name": "retrieve", "start_ms": 0.9, "end_ms": 1.7, "model": null, "outcome": "1 search", "detail": {"query": "How are the positional encodings built, and why sinusoids rather than learned embeddings?", "papers": null, "k": 4, "evidence": {"best": 0.516, "union": 0.516, "top_bm25": 22.628, "query_terms": 7}}}, {"name": "decide", "start_ms": 1.7, "end_ms": 1.7, "model": null, "outcome": "draft", "detail": {"best": 0.516, "union": 0.516, "top_bm25": 22.628, "query_terms": 7}}, {"name": "draft", "start_ms": 1.7, "end_ms": 7104.9, "model": null, "outcome": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "detail": {"level": "full"}}, {"name": "wait:draft", "start_ms": 1.7, "end_ms": 6134.3, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "outcome": "granted", "detail": {"waited_s": 6.141}}, {"name": "call:draft", "start_ms": 6134.3, "end_ms": 7104.9, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "outcome": "200:ok", "detail": {}}, {"name": "check", "start_ms": 7104.9, "end_ms": 7105.4, "model": null, "outcome": "pass", "detail": {"gate_ok": true, "failures": 0, "verifier": null}}, {"name": "verify", "start_ms": 7105.4, "end_ms": 7105.4, "model": null, "outcome": "off (config)", "detail": {}}, {"name": "send", "start_ms": 7105.4, "end_ms": 7105.4, "model": null, "outcome": "answer", "detail": {}}], "checks": {"gate": {"ok": true, "sentences": 4, "failures": []}, "verifier": null, "draft_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "attempts": 1, "retrieval": {"query": "How are the positional encodings built, and why sinusoids rather than learned embeddings?", "papers": null, "k": 4, "pids": ["attention:600:0033", "attention:600:0049", "attention:600:0035", "attention:600:0034"]}}, "released_ms": 7105.4, "budget_wait_ms": 6132.6, "tokens_in": 761, "tokens_out": 261, "level_name": "full"}}
{"type": "answer", "run_id": "retrieval-part2-lean-20261110", "scenario": "eval:retrieval", "source": "real", "setting": "small_lean", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 600, "k": 4, "rerank": false, "router": false}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q4", "request_id": "retrieval-part2-lean-20261110-small_lean-gpt-oss-120b-Q4", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:25:34.782+00:00", "degraded": false, "reply": {"request_id": "retrieval-part2-lean-20261110-small_lean-gpt-oss-120b-Q4", "question": "Per Table 1, how does self-attention compare with recurrent layers on complexity per layer, sequential operations and maximum path length?", "kind": "answer", "level": 0, "text": "According to Table 1, a self‑attention layer has a per‑layer computational complexity of \\(O(n^{2}\\,d)\\) while a recurrent layer requires \\(O(n\\,d^{2})\\) [S2].  \nSelf‑attention needs only a constant number of sequential operations per layer ( \\(O(1)\\) ), whereas a recurrent layer must perform \\(O(n)\\) sequential operations [S1][S2].  \nFinally, the maximum path length between any two positions is \\(O(1)\\) for self‑attention but \\(O(n)\\) for recurrent layers [S2].", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "1706.03762v7 p.6 §4", "pid": "attention:600:0039", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p06-b013", "attention-p06-b014"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "1706.03762v7 p.6 §3.4", "pid": "attention:600:0032", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p06-b001", "attention-p06-b002"]}, {"sid": "S3", "cite": "1706.03762v7 p.6 §4", "pid": "attention:600:0037", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p06-b012"]}, {"sid": "S4", "cite": "1706.03762v7 p.6 §4", "pid": "attention:600:0036", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p06-b011"]}], "notice": "checked for citations only (no second-model check)", "eta_s": null, "model_calls": [{"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 683, "completion_tokens": 180, "tokens_estimated